{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof that for P = N(-mu, 1) and Q = N(mu, 1) truncated to an interval [a, b] (a < b), or to any interval of positive length, d_H^2(P,Q) <= d_H(P,Q) <= d_TV(P,Q) with d_TV = (1/2)||P - Q||_1 and d_H^2 = (1/2)||sqrt P - sqrt Q||_2^2, strictly d_H < d_TV for mu != 0, which answers MathOverflow question 184460 positively; and the inequality behind it: for a log-concave f >= 0 on R with f cosh integrable and integral of f sinh zero, (int f cosh)(int f cosh - int f) <= (int f |sinh|)^2, strictly for strictly log-concave f.",
